komodo: UFS encoding modes, NEXUS_TYPE, auto-retry and register dumps

First hardware run (0086, byte-granular): TEST UNIT READY timed out x3. zuma's DT
has fixed-prdt-req_list-ocs; Linux sets HCI_UTRL_NEXUS_TYPE for SCSI slots.
boot-arg ufsmode (bit0 byte offsets, bit1 4K PRDT, bit2 NEXUS), default 0x6;
on timeout flip bit0 and retry; dump HCI/UIC/vendor registers.

